{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetMoh1kUX98ZrApKvcTU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that transitions an order to `CANCELLED` status, cancels its `CREATED` shipments, handles error cases (404 for non-existent, 409 if any shipment is `CONFIRMED`), and prevents creating shipments for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-23` — Order data class lacks a status field\n- `OrderRepository.kt:11-27` — In-memory store with save/findById/findAll\n- `OrderController.kt:17-46` — POST /orders creates, GET /orders/{id} reads, GET /orders lists\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` — Shipment has `ShipmentStatus` enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — In-memory store, no method to find shipments by orderId\n- `ShipmentController.kt:22-56` — POST /shipments creates (no order status check), GET endpoints\n- `ApiExceptions.kt` — ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — Converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions in this repository:**\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError responses\n- Responses include `$.error.code`, `$.error.message`, `$.error.fields`\n- POST creates return 201 CREATED via `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED)`\n- Tests verify both status and error envelope via jsonPath\n- Repositories are injected and return entities or null\n- Order creation does not store a status; newly created orders need status `ACTIVE`\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — Add `status: OrderStatus` field (cannot avoid; requirement mandates status)\n2. `OrderStatus.kt` — New enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED (required for Order)\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` — Add method to find shipments by orderId to cancel them (required for cancel logic)\n4. `OrderController.kt` — Add `POST /{orderId}/cancel` endpoint (requirement)\n5. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Add `findByOrderId()` method (required by cancel logic)\n6. `ShipmentController.kt` — Check order status in create(), reject 409 if CANCELLED (requirement)\n7. `ApiError.kt` — Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code (required for shipment creation rejection)\n8. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Add cancel endpoint tests (required for AC 3, 4, 5)\n9. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add test for creating shipment on cancelled order (required for AC 5)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order is immutable data class; cancellation must create new instance and re-save\n- Concurrent modifications: shipments could change status between reading and writing; mitigation: in-memory map, single-threaded test execution\n- ShipmentRepository lacks orderId index; scanning all shipments O(n) for each cancel, acceptable for benchmark\n- Need to ensure all-or-nothing semantics: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, cancel fails and nothing changes\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What ErrorCode should creating a shipment for a cancelled order use? (Not specified, but 409 is required)\n  → Decision: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum (consistent with `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS` naming)\n- Can the same response body that creates an order also include status?\n  → Yes; data class serialization includes all fields; adding `status` to Order automatically includes it in JSON responses\n- Should updating an order require versioning/optimistic locking?\n  → No; the in-memory implementation has no concurrency control; tests run serially\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **New file: `OrderStatus.kt`** — Define enum `OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }` with Kotlin enum syntax. Placed alongside Order.kt.\n\n2. **`Order.kt`** — Add field `val status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` to the data class. All existing code continues to work; the field serializes in JSON. Tests pass because they don't check status field (yet).\n\n3. **`OrderRepository.kt`** — Add two methods:\n   - `fun findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` — would require importing ShipmentRepository, creating a circular dependency. *This approach rejected.*\n   - *Better approach:* Inject `ShipmentRepository` into `OrderController`, not the repository layer, and let controller call it. Keeps repositories decoupled. But Order.cancel() logic needs to happen somewhere — either in controller or a service.\n   - *Chosen approach:* Inject `ShipmentRepository` into `OrderController` as a second dependency. The cancel() method in controller fetches shipments by orderId using new repository method (see below), checks for CONFIRMED, cancels CREATED shipments, updates order.\n\n4. **`ShipmentRepository.kt`** — Add method `fun findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment> = store.values.filter { it.orderId == orderId }`. Scans all shipments; acceptable for in-memory benchmark.\n\n5. **`OrderController.kt`** — Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint:\n   - Get order by orderId; throw 404 if not found\n   - If order already CANCELLED, return 200 OK with unchanged order (idempotent)\n   - Fetch all shipments for orderId using `shipmentRepository.findByOrderId()`\n   - Check if any shipment has status CONFIRMED; if so, throw ConflictException(409) with appropriate code\n   - Set shipments with status CREATED to CANCELLED\n   - Save updated shipments to repository\n   - Update order status to CANCELLED\n   - Return 200 OK with updated order\n\n6. **`ShipmentController.kt`** — In create(), after checking shipment doesn't exist:\n   - Fetch order from orderRepository by orderId\n   - If order exists and has status CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(409) with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n   - If order doesn't exist, allow creation (preserve current behavior: shipments can exist for non-existent orders)\n\n7. **`ApiError.kt`** — Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum. This code is returned when attempting to create a shipment for a cancelled order.\n\n8. **`OrderControllerTest.kt`** — Add test cases:\n   - Cancel active order: verify status 200, order.status = CANCELLED, shipments with status CREATED are now CANCELLED\n   - Cancel already cancelled order: verify status 200, nothing changes (idempotent)\n   - Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment: verify status 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n   - Cancel non-existent order: verify status 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n\n9. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** — Add test case:\n   - Create shipment for cancelled order: verify status 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n\n1. *Add status to Order via a separate OrderStatusProvider service* — Rejected: adds unnecessary indirection; Order entity should own its status.\n\n2. *Make cancel logic a separate OrderService* — Rejected: not required; controller can handle it inline. For a real system this would be best, but ticket allows simple controller logic.\n\n3. *Return 200 OK instead of idempotent success for already-cancelled order* — Rejected: requirement explicitly says \"Cancelling an order that is already CANCELLED succeeds and changes nothing\", implying idempotent success, not error.\n\n4. *Add ORDER_CANCELLED as an exception subclass instead of ErrorCode* — Rejected: consistent with existing pattern (all errors use ApiException subclasses + ErrorCode enum).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Check | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Cancel active order | Order by orderId, Shipments by orderId | No CONFIRMED shipments | Order.status→CANCELLED, Shipments.status CREATED→CANCELLED | 200 Order | Return order body |\n| Retry cancel (already CANCELLED) | Order by orderId | Order.status=CANCELLED (no-op) | None | 200 Order | Return unchanged order |\n| Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED | Order by orderId, Shipments by orderId | Any CONFIRMED found | None | 409 ConflictException(ORDER_CONFIRMED) | GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns ApiError |\n| Cancel non-existent | Order by orderId not found | — | — | 404 ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND) | GlobalExceptionHandler catches |\n| Create shipment for cancelled order | Order by orderId | Order.status=CANCELLED | None | 409 ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) | GlobalExceptionHandler catches |\n| Create shipment for non-existent order | Order by orderId not found | — | Shipment saved | 201 Shipment | Preserves current behavior |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest** new tests:\n   - `cancelActiveOrderCancelsOrderAndCreatedShipments()` — Create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel order, verify order.status=CANCELLED, verify shipment.status=CANCELLED\n   - `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent()` — Create order, cancel it, cancel it again, verify 200 and order unchanged\n   - `cancelOrderBlockedByConfirmedShipmentChangesNothing()` — Create order, create CONFIRMED shipment (directly via repository), attempt cancel, verify 409, verify order.status still ACTIVE, verify shipment.status still CONFIRMED\n   - `cancelNonExistentOrderReturns404()` — Attempt cancel on non-existent orderId, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n   \n2. **ShipmentControllerTest** new test:\n   - `createShipmentForCancelledOrderReturns409()` — Create order, cancel it, attempt create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\nAll existing tests must pass unchanged (AC 2).\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the design. Starting with the new OrderStatus enum:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":23330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":316},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd0a0a31-c8f9-4034-bbc8-5a421c2528b1","uuid":"584507c4-21a4-4cfb-b334-dc9285a3ca5d","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:44:34.800Z","request_id":"req_011CetMogNJsd8xE1jrsM1tu"}
