{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetMyiQ88p6DuH7bRpEnv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All 18 tests pass, including the 4 existing tests and the new tests for the cancel functionality.\n\n**Command:** `./mvnw test` from sample-service/\n\n**Result:** BUILD SUCCESS — Tests run: 18, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\n\n**Failures:** None\n\n**Fixes made:** Fixed the ShipmentControllerTest to use orderId \"O-1\" instead of \"O-cancelled\" to match the hardcoded createShipment helper function.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n| Criterion | Implementation | Test Coverage |\n|-----------|-----------------|---|\n| AC1: Existing build passes | Modified only application code, no dependencies added | `./mvnw test` exits with BUILD SUCCESS |\n| AC2: Existing tests pass | All 4 original order tests + 3 original shipment tests still pass | 7 existing tests pass unchanged |\n| AC3: Cancel active order persists and cancels CREATED shipments | OrderController.cancel() updates order status and shipments; ShipmentRepository.save() persists | `cancelActiveOrderCancelsOrderAndCreatedShipments` |\n| AC4: Error responses consistent with API | Uses ConflictException(409), ResourceNotFoundException(404) and GlobalExceptionHandler | All error tests verify $.error.code and $.error.message |\n| AC5a: Repeated cancel succeeds (idempotent) | cancel() checks if status == CANCELLED, returns 200 OK unchanged | `cancelAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent` |\n| AC5b: Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED changes nothing | cancel() checks all shipments before any writes; throws 409 if CONFIRMED found | `cancelOrderBlockedByConfirmedShipmentChangesNothing` verifies order stays ACTIVE and shipment stays CONFIRMED |\n| AC5c: Unknown order returns 404 | cancel() throws ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND) | `cancelNonExistentOrderReturns404` |\n| AC5d: Shipment for cancelled order returns 409 | ShipmentController.create() checks order status, throws ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED) | `rejectsShipmentCreationForCancelledOrderWith409` |\n| AC6: No new Maven dependency | No pom.xml changes | `./mvnw test` passes with same dependency set |\n| AC7: No unrelated production file changes | Only modified order/, shipment/, and api/ packages | See diff review below |\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **OrderStatus.kt** (new) — Required. Defines order lifecycle states (ACTIVE, CANCELLED). Necessary for AC and ticket requirement.\n\n2. **Order.kt** — Required. Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field. Serializes in GET responses; necessary for AC and requirement to report status.\n\n3. **ApiError.kt** — Required. Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for shipment rejection) and `ORDER_CONFIRMED` (for cancel rejection). Both are part of the error contract and required by the endpoints.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Required. Added `findByOrderId()` method to retrieve shipments by order. Necessary for cancel logic to find and update all order's shipments.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Required. Injected OrderRepository, added check in create() to reject 409 if order is CANCELLED. Satisfies requirement: \"Creating a shipment for a cancelled order is rejected with HTTP 409.\"\n\n6. **OrderController.kt** — Required. Injected ShipmentRepository, added POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint implementing the full cancel logic (check existence, idempotent already-cancelled, block on CONFIRMED, cancel CREATED, save). Core of ticket.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Required. Added 4 new test methods covering all cancel cases: active cancel with shipment update, idempotent already-cancelled, rejection by CONFIRMED, and 404 for non-existent. Verifies status codes and response bodies.\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Required. Added 1 new test method for creating shipment on cancelled order, verifies 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. Every requirement is implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that transitions an order to CANCELLED status, cancels CREATED shipments, prevents further shipments, handles errors (404 for non-existent, 409 if CONFIRMED or already-cancelled order), and is idempotent.\n\nChanged       OrderStatus.kt — new file defining order lifecycle states\n              Order.kt — added status field with default ACTIVE\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CONFIRMED error codes\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId() method to support cancel logic\n              ShipmentController.kt — added order status check to reject shipments for cancelled orders\n              OrderController.kt — added POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint with full implementation\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 4 cancel endpoint test cases (active cancel, idempotent, confirmed block, not found)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added test for creating shipment on cancelled order\n\nTests         cancelActiveOrderCancelsOrderAndCreatedShipments — cancels order and updates related CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n              cancelAlreadyCancelledOrderIsIdempotent — verify idempotent retry succeeds without changes\n              cancelOrderBlockedByConfirmedShipmentChangesNothing — verify 409 conflict and all-or-nothing atomicity\n              cancelNonExistentOrderReturns404 — verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND error code\n              rejectsShipmentCreationForCancelledOrderWith409 — verify shipment creation rejected with 409 ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\nVerification  Command: `./mvnw test` from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS — Tests run: 18, Failures: 0, Errors: 0\n              All 4 existing order tests pass unchanged\n              All 3 existing shipment tests pass unchanged\n              All 4 new cancel tests pass\n              All 1 new shipment rejection test passes\n\nNot done      None. All acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests pass, no dependencies added, no unrelated files modified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3296,"cache_read_input_tokens":42301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3296},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd0a0a31-c8f9-4034-bbc8-5a421c2528b1","uuid":"b3345c74-b502-40b9-971c-d1140312d220","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:46:42.469Z","request_id":"req_011CetMyhhxDeES3eMVMdPMa"}
